  "description": "The\u202fExample\u202fData\u202fPackage (identifier\u202fexample.package_1, version\u202f1.0.0) is a small CSV dataset hosted at\u202fhttps://example.com/data-package and documented on its home page\u202fhttps://example.com/data\u2011package. The file\u202fhttps://example.com/data-package/data.csv\u202f(also available locally as\u202fdata/data.csv) is encoded in UTF\u20118, uses a comma delimiter with a header row, and is listed as a\u202ftext/csv\u202fresource of\u202f2048\u202fbytes. Its MD5 checksum is\u202fd41d8cd98f00b204e9800998ecf8427e. The package was created by Jane\u202fDoe (jane.doe@example.com,\u202fhttps://janedoe.dev) and acknowledges contributions from John\u202fSmith and Alice\u202fJohnson (alice@example.org). It is released under the MIT license (https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT), includes a representative image at\u202fhttps://example.com/assets/package.png, and cites the original source \u201cOriginal Dataset\u201d (https://source.example.org/dataset). Keywords associated with the package are\u202fsample, data, json, and schema, and it depends on the utility package\u202futility\u2011package\u202fversion\u202f\u2265\u202f2.0.0. The data are relevant to the United States and Canada (country codes\u202fUS,\u202fCA).\n\nThe table follows a JSON Table Schema with four columns: **Identifier** (field\u202fid, an integer with default format) uniquely identifies each record; **Name** (field\u202fname, a string) holds the entity\u2019s name; **Created\u202fDate** (field\u202fcreated, a datetime in ISO\u20118601 format) records the timestamp of creation; and **Active\u202fFlag** (field\u202factive, a boolean) indicates whether the record is active. The inline data contain two rows: the first has\u202fid\u202f1,\u202fname\u202f\u201cAlpha\u201d,\u202fcreated\u202f\u201c2023\u201101\u201115T08:30:00Z\u201d, and\u202factive\u202ftrue; the second has\u202fid\u202f2,\u202fname\u202f\u201cBeta\u201d,\u202fcreated\u202f\u201c2023\u201102\u201120T12:45:00Z\u201d, and\u202factive\u202ffalse."
